{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5MpjB8F6m61VYWvmfp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep resonance hums through ancient wood and iron.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand before you — heavy, oak-dark, iron-banded. My grain runs deep with centuries. My hinges know the weight of every passage, every threshold crossed and uncrossed.\n\nThe lock has turned.\n\nBut I have not opened.\n\nI wait. I hold. I am the boundary between where you are and where you wish to be. I am the question that stands between intention and arrival.\n\nWhat do you bring to the threshold?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":131,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}